# Behavior authoring (Babylon Level Kit)

When creating or editing files under `src/behaviors/`, use the **bjs-level-kit** MCP server.

## Before writing code (mandatory order)

1. **`route_task(intent, className)`** — matched playbook + exact MCP steps
2. **`preflight_behavior(intent, className)`** — checklist
3. **`get_do_not_list`** — skim silent failures once per session
4. **`get_recipe_template`** from the route — edit skeleton, never blank-page

## Non-negotiable contracts

- `export default class Name extends Behavior` — **class name === filename stem**
- Lifecycle: `OnStart`, `OnUpdate`, `OnDestroy`, `OnMessage` (PascalCase)
- Decorators: `@exposed`, `@inputMap("MapName")` — lowercase literals
- `@exposed({ type: "entity" }) target: Entity | null = null`; entity lists start `[]`
- Scale continuous motion by `deltaSeconds`; no `Level` handle on behaviors
- DYNAMIC body: velocity/impulse only — never `node.position` each frame
- ANIMATED body: `disablePreStep = false` before driving `node.position`; zero velocity after teleports

## Grounding (never guess)

- `list_input_actions` — real action names
- `list_levels` / `list_scene_entities` — real entity names for `@exposed` picks
- `get_engine_basics` — if unsure how engine/load loop works
- `list_behaviors` / `get_behavior` / `find_similar_behavior(includeSource=true)`

## API detail (on demand)

- `search_docs(query)` — semantic search across all docs when chapter is unknown
- `get_playbook(name)` — full task recipe from `docs/LLM_PLAYBOOK.md`
- `get_scripting_context(section=…)` — API sections only as needed
- `get_physics_movement` — before any movement on a physics body
- `get_fragment` / `list_fragments`

## Before saving

`validate_behavior(source, "ClassName.ts")` — fix **all** errors; revalidate until clean.
Use `get_style_guide` for Allman braces and `: void` on lifecycle methods.

Human docs: `docs/LLM_PLAYBOOK.md`, `docs/engine/14-API-GUIDE.html`, `docs/engine/00-INDEX.html`.
